id=a52sxq_settings_search_semantic_off
name=Settings search: no on-device semantic ("in-app assist") indexing
author=kusti420
description=SecSettingsIntelligence's in-app assist (natural-language Settings results, SSESearchManager) embeds all 1076 DQA help texts through Semantic Search Core's CPU TFLite encoder (0.72 s per batch of 50, about 13 minutes) inside the SearchActivity process, every time search opens: the worker is a plain thread, the process is killed as cached ~10 s after the user leaves search, setIndexingStarted() has already cleared indexedLanguage, so the next open sees isLanguageChanged/isIndexingCanceled, deletes the index ("VectorIndex: Reset completed") and starts again from record 0. It never finishes unless search stays open for 13 minutes; measured 8+ minutes of continuous CPU after one open (sweep 2026-10-29). Designed for the NPU encoder of the S26 Ultra. The gate Rune.getSupportSearchInAppAssist() is a build-time literal ("510" >= 400); this makes it false, so no indexing, no per-query embedding and no semantic result group. Keyword Settings search, Finder and My Files semantic search (semantic_search_core) are unchanged. UNTESTED-ON-DEVICE: verify with logcat -s SSESearchManager VectorIndex MultiLangModelInferencing while opening Settings search (expect silence) and "semanticSearchSupported : false" / no "inference MultiLang" lines.
